WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.300 --> 00:00:03.767
-Thank you
for being here, Nathan Lane.

00:00:03.767 --> 00:00:06.701
-It's so nice to be here,
James DeSantis-Fallon.

00:00:06.701 --> 00:00:10.200
It's so good to see you.

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:13.901
And may I say, the Ozempic is
doing wonders for your figure.

00:00:13.901 --> 00:00:15.334
-[ Laughs ] Thank you.

00:00:15.334 --> 00:00:20.167
-You have the taut physique
of a Lindsey Graham pool boy.

00:00:20.167 --> 00:00:23.000
How many Kegels
are you up to now?

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:24.767
You know,
I love doing your show,

00:00:24.767 --> 00:00:26.300
because of all
the late-night shows,

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:28.434
yours is the closest
cab ride from my apartment.

00:00:28.434 --> 00:00:30.167
-Oh, that's so sweet.
That's so nice of you.

00:00:30.167 --> 00:00:32.734
-But you astound me.

00:00:32.734 --> 00:00:35.067
You're a talk-show host,
a game-show host,

00:00:35.067 --> 00:00:36.467
a children's book author.

00:00:36.467 --> 00:00:40.434
Let me ask you a question.
Are things okay at home?

00:00:40.434 --> 00:00:41.868
Seriously.
-Yes.

00:00:41.868 --> 00:00:45.200
-I am so thrilled to spend
my one night off talking to you

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:47.434
and then performing later
with Lil Uzi Vert.

00:00:47.434 --> 00:00:48.701
-Wait.

00:00:48.701 --> 00:00:51.434
-Because, as you know,
we always travel together,

00:00:51.434 --> 00:00:55.033
because I sing a lil backup
for lil, but just a lil.

00:00:55.033 --> 00:00:57.000
-Just a lil?

00:00:57.000 --> 00:00:58.734
Just a lil.
-Yeah.

00:00:58.734 --> 00:01:01.334
-Yeah, I was trying to remember
the last time we saw each other.

00:01:01.334 --> 00:01:03.267
-I believe the last time
we hung out was

00:01:03.267 --> 00:01:06.300
Nick Cannon's
40th...baby shower?

00:01:06.300 --> 00:01:09.968
[ Laughter ]

00:01:09.968 --> 00:01:12.767
-That's exactly --
That's exactly right.

00:01:12.767 --> 00:01:15.801
-No, wait. No, wait.
I saw you last week.

00:01:15.801 --> 00:01:17.567
You were out protesting Trump's
impending indictment.

00:01:17.567 --> 00:01:18.601
-That's right. Yes.

00:01:18.601 --> 00:01:20.501
-Yes, you had you
had that lovely tailored

00:01:20.501 --> 00:01:23.100
"Let's Go, Brandon" T-shirt.

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:24.434
But speaking of Trump, you know,

00:01:24.434 --> 00:01:27.567
I was recently hired to become
his new legal adviser.

00:01:27.567 --> 00:01:29.901
Hear me out.

00:01:29.901 --> 00:01:35.000
You know, they were looking for
a very friendly TV lawyer,

00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:36.834
and then they heard
I had won a Tony Award

00:01:36.834 --> 00:01:38.300
for playing
Trump's favorite lawyer,

00:01:38.300 --> 00:01:40.067
Roy Cohn,
in "Angels in America,"

00:01:40.067 --> 00:01:41.434
so they thought I'd be perfect.

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:45.200
That and everybody else said,
"Not a chance in hell."

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:46.601
-But do you know
anything about the law?

00:01:46.601 --> 00:01:48.400
-No, but neither does
Rudy Giuliani,

00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:53.100
so what does it matter?

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:56.467
Look, believe me,
I tried to say no,

00:01:56.467 --> 00:02:01.367
but my goodness, that Mar-a-Lago
has one hell of a waffle bar.

00:02:01.367 --> 00:02:03.334
-Oh, is that right?
-Yeah.

00:02:03.334 --> 00:02:04.901
And, look, it's not too bad
working for Trump,

00:02:04.901 --> 00:02:06.300
although, occasionally,
I do have

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:08.267
to jiggle some keys in his face

00:02:08.267 --> 00:02:09.801
like a cat
to get his attention.

00:02:09.801 --> 00:02:10.968
-Yeah.

00:02:10.968 --> 00:02:12.367
-I feel sorry for him,
actually,

00:02:12.367 --> 00:02:15.100
because, you know, just before
the authorities busted in,

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:16.367
Melania turned to him
and said,

00:02:16.367 --> 00:02:17.434
"You know what?

00:02:17.434 --> 00:02:19.501
I'm finally in the mood."

00:02:19.501 --> 00:02:22.334
-[ Laughs ] What a bummer.

00:02:22.334 --> 00:02:24.968
-It's not looking good
for Trump, though.

00:02:24.968 --> 00:02:27.634
I've already asked to borrow
Harvey Weinstein's

00:02:27.634 --> 00:02:31.701
sympathy walker,
and I'm giving him some

00:02:31.701 --> 00:02:36.901
prison survival tips,
because, as you know,

00:02:36.901 --> 00:02:38.934
I did a stint in Rikers
in the '80s

00:02:38.934 --> 00:02:41.667
for stealing a French baguette
for a big fondue party.

00:02:41.667 --> 00:02:44.400
-[ Laughs ] Oh, my goodness.

00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:46.234
-Hey, but I'm really
feeling like Trump's lawyer,

00:02:46.234 --> 00:02:48.734
mainly because
he hasn't paid me.

00:02:48.734 --> 00:02:50.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:50.367 --> 00:02:52.100
-Wow. Well, no, get over here.
Come on.

00:02:52.100 --> 00:02:53.234
♪♪
No. No, don't leave.

00:02:53.234 --> 00:02:54.300
No. No, no. Wait.

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:56.467
No, we're not done.
We're not done.

00:02:56.467 --> 00:02:58.868
We're not done.
No, we're not done.

00:02:58.868 --> 00:03:00.968
Wow! Nathan Lane.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:00.968 --> 00:03:03.467
-Oh!
-Come on!

00:03:03.467 --> 00:03:06.033
-Who comes out, who brings it
like you bring it?

00:03:06.033 --> 00:03:08.367
And you're -- I'm happy because
you're a busy, busy man.

00:03:08.367 --> 00:03:09.834
-I'm so busy.
-You are.

00:03:09.834 --> 00:03:11.267
-You actually told me
you're going to attend

00:03:11.267 --> 00:03:12.300
King Charles' coronation.

00:03:12.300 --> 00:03:14.734
-Oh, yeah.
Chuck and I go way back.

00:03:14.734 --> 00:03:15.868
-"Chuck."

00:03:15.868 --> 00:03:17.367
-Because we were chums at the

00:03:17.367 --> 00:03:21.334
Pemberley Finishing School
for Sophisticated Boys.

00:03:21.334 --> 00:03:22.467
-That's a hard school
to get into.

00:03:22.467 --> 00:03:25.100
-Oh, yeah,
very hard school to get into.

00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:27.801
You know...
[ Laughter ]

00:03:27.801 --> 00:03:31.234
You know, I am thrilled about
going to the coronation

00:03:31.234 --> 00:03:33.567
because I haven't been
in Buckingham Palace

00:03:33.567 --> 00:03:35.701
since I was a referee
for one of the queen's

00:03:35.701 --> 00:03:37.434
underground corgi fights.

00:03:37.434 --> 00:03:39.067
-Oh, I've heard of about those.

00:03:39.067 --> 00:03:40.267
-Oh, those were brutal.

00:03:40.267 --> 00:03:41.567
-Yeah, I heard about those.
-Yeah.

00:03:41.567 --> 00:03:44.400
-I wanted to say congrats to
you, in all seriousness,

00:03:44.400 --> 00:03:47.567
in all honesty,
because you won an Emmy Award --

00:03:47.567 --> 00:03:50.267
and well-deserved -- for
"Only Murders in the Building."

00:03:50.267 --> 00:03:53.567
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yes. Thank you.

00:03:55.901 --> 00:03:57.200
Thank you.
-Well-deserved.

00:03:57.200 --> 00:03:58.467
-Well, thank you.

00:03:58.467 --> 00:04:03.100
Yes, I -- yes, I became
the most Emmy-nominated

00:04:03.100 --> 00:04:07.000
guest actor in history
and finally won

00:04:07.000 --> 00:04:08.467
the big-boy Primetime Emmy.

00:04:08.467 --> 00:04:09.634
-Wow.

00:04:09.634 --> 00:04:11.634
-I -- Technically,
it's not my first Emmy.

00:04:11.634 --> 00:04:13.100
I do have two Daytime Emmys,

00:04:13.100 --> 00:04:15.133
but, as you know,
they're filled with chocolate

00:04:15.133 --> 00:04:17.467
and not taken quite
as seriously.

00:04:17.467 --> 00:04:19.801
But, you know,
as you also know,

00:04:19.801 --> 00:04:21.968
because you've beaten me
in this category,

00:04:21.968 --> 00:04:24.300
they give out
the guest-actor awards

00:04:24.300 --> 00:04:26.734
at the Creative Arts ceremony
the week before.

00:04:26.734 --> 00:04:31.701
And having lost six times,
I was hesitant to fly

00:04:31.701 --> 00:04:33.734
all the way
to Los Angeles and lose again.

00:04:33.734 --> 00:04:35.334
And everybody told me,
"Don't go.

00:04:35.334 --> 00:04:37.100
Wait and see if you win,
and if you do,

00:04:37.100 --> 00:04:39.701
you'll be
invited to the 'real Emmys'

00:04:39.701 --> 00:04:42.067
and they'll introduce you
as the guest-actor winner

00:04:42.067 --> 00:04:44.167
and you'll get to
present an award

00:04:44.167 --> 00:04:46.601
to someone who's obviously
more important than you

00:04:46.601 --> 00:04:48.834
because they're getting
their award on television."

00:04:48.834 --> 00:04:50.133
-Wow.

00:04:50.133 --> 00:04:53.133
-So I said, "Yeah, yeah,
that's what I'm going to do."

00:04:53.133 --> 00:04:54.267
So I didn't go.

00:04:54.267 --> 00:04:56.300
I finally won the award
this year,

00:04:56.300 --> 00:04:57.734
they did away
with that tradition,

00:04:57.734 --> 00:05:00.067
and I wasn't invited
to the ceremony.

00:05:00.067 --> 00:05:01.234
[ Laughter ]

00:05:01.234 --> 00:05:05.167
-Yeah! That's the best.
-Yeah.

00:05:05.167 --> 00:05:09.200
So, my Emmy win
was a closely guarded secret,

00:05:09.200 --> 00:05:11.067
right up there
with Ron DeSantis'

00:05:11.067 --> 00:05:12.534
OnlyFans password.

00:05:12.534 --> 00:05:15.901
-Yeah. I wanted to talk to you
about this,

00:05:15.901 --> 00:05:17.000
"Pictures from Home."

00:05:17.000 --> 00:05:18.133
You're on Broadway.
-Oh, yeah.

00:05:18.133 --> 00:05:21.100
-Oh, I mean, gosh,
you're the best.

00:05:21.100 --> 00:05:22.834
This is your 25th play?

00:05:22.834 --> 00:05:26.567
-Yes, it's my -- Five more
and I'm up for parole.

00:05:26.567 --> 00:05:29.667
No, this is a beautiful
play by Sharr White called

00:05:29.667 --> 00:05:30.934
"Pictures from Home."

00:05:30.934 --> 00:05:32.634
It's a very funny,
very moving play

00:05:32.634 --> 00:05:35.767
directed by Bartlett Sher
and starring the brilliant

00:05:35.767 --> 00:05:37.434
Danny Burstein
and Zoe Wanamaker.

00:05:37.434 --> 00:05:39.834
It's based on this
extraordinary photo memoir

00:05:39.834 --> 00:05:42.801
by the celebrated
photographer Larry Sultan,

00:05:42.801 --> 00:05:44.501
who, for a period
of 10 years,

00:05:44.501 --> 00:05:46.901
photographed his parents
and interviewed them.

00:05:46.901 --> 00:05:50.267
And the play is about the
last two years of that process.

00:05:50.267 --> 00:05:52.100
And the audiences
have been loving it.

00:05:52.100 --> 00:05:55.901
I'm sure you'll come see it once
Marty Short takes over for me.

00:05:55.901 --> 00:05:58.367
[ Laughter ]

00:05:58.367 --> 00:06:02.000
But, as you know, it's,
yes, my 25th Broadway play.

00:06:02.000 --> 00:06:03.133
It was worth it

00:06:03.133 --> 00:06:06.934
just to get that 10%
discount at Sardi's.

00:06:06.934 --> 00:06:08.834
-Did they give you 10%?
-Yeah, they do.

00:06:08.834 --> 00:06:11.133
I would put the brakes on
and work less,

00:06:11.133 --> 00:06:13.801
but, as you know, I have
a crippling gambling addiction.

00:06:13.801 --> 00:06:15.734
-Oh.
-I bet on corgi fights.

00:06:15.734 --> 00:06:16.834
-Oh, yeah, I know.
I heard about this.

00:06:16.834 --> 00:06:18.567
I heard about this.
-Yes.

00:06:18.567 --> 00:06:20.267
-Now, if this wasn't
enough, though,

00:06:20.267 --> 00:06:21.968
you have a film opening up
April 21st.

00:06:21.968 --> 00:06:24.200
-Oh, yes. This is big.

00:06:24.200 --> 00:06:25.968
-"Beau is Afraid"
starring Joaquin Phoenix.

00:06:25.968 --> 00:06:26.968
-Yes.

00:06:26.968 --> 00:06:29.701
-They just put
the poster online,

00:06:29.701 --> 00:06:32.033
and it went viral
on Twitter and the socials.

00:06:32.033 --> 00:06:33.367
People are excited
about this movie.

00:06:33.367 --> 00:06:36.567
-Let me just say,
"Cocaine Bear" it's not.

00:06:36.567 --> 00:06:38.968
-Wow! Yeah.
Thank you for clearing that up.

00:06:38.968 --> 00:06:41.834
-This is more in the
art-house genre.

00:06:41.834 --> 00:06:45.501
It is a masterful piece

00:06:45.501 --> 00:06:48.467
of filmmaking by the brilliant
Ari Aster,

00:06:48.467 --> 00:06:52.400
who gave us "Hereditary"
and "Midsommar," also for A24.

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:54.734
And I've been --
-How was Joaquin?

00:06:54.734 --> 00:06:56.601
-Oh, Joaquin is brilliant.
-Yeah, he's great.

00:06:56.601 --> 00:06:58.033
-You know, he's just,

00:06:58.033 --> 00:07:00.667
I think, the finest actor
working in films today.

00:07:00.667 --> 00:07:02.734
And I like to call it
the Jewish

00:07:02.734 --> 00:07:04.167
"Everything Everywhere
All at Once."

00:07:04.167 --> 00:07:05.534
-Oh, wow.

00:07:05.534 --> 00:07:09.367
-Because it's an epic tale
of guilt and codependency,

00:07:09.367 --> 00:07:11.300
the story of my life.

00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:15.100
It is one man's surreal,

00:07:15.100 --> 00:07:19.100
nightmarish odyssey to get home
to see his mother.

00:07:19.100 --> 00:07:20.701
I would call it Kafkaesque,

00:07:20.701 --> 00:07:22.334
but then I'd have
to explain Kafka,

00:07:22.334 --> 00:07:23.534
and we'd be here all night.

00:07:23.534 --> 00:07:24.667
-Yeah, thank you.
I appreciate that.

00:07:24.667 --> 00:07:30.167
-But it's an
unbelievable piece of work

00:07:30.167 --> 00:07:31.834
by Ari and Joaquin.

00:07:31.834 --> 00:07:33.400
And, you know, it's funny.

00:07:33.400 --> 00:07:35.334
He and I -- Joaquin --
we really hit it off,

00:07:35.334 --> 00:07:37.634
although we have
very different sensibilities.

00:07:37.634 --> 00:07:41.901
You know, he's very intense,
and I'm just tense.

00:07:41.901 --> 00:07:43.667
But he thought I was funny,

00:07:43.667 --> 00:07:46.000
so every time we did a take,
you know, he would say,

00:07:46.000 --> 00:07:49.200
"I can't look you directly
in the eyes or I'll break up."

00:07:49.200 --> 00:07:52.767
So just know that in every
close-up and in a scene with me,

00:07:52.767 --> 00:07:55.534
he's just looking
directly at my nose.

00:07:55.534 --> 00:07:56.767
-I cannot wait to see it.

00:07:56.767 --> 00:07:58.934
I'm so happy every single time
to see you.

00:07:58.934 --> 00:08:01.534
You're a gentleman
and you're one of the best.

00:08:01.534 --> 00:08:04.267
One of the best ever to do it.
Nathan Lane, everybody.

00:08:04.267 --> 00:08:08.033
"Beau is Afraid"
opens April 21st.

00:08:08.033 --> 00:08:09.834
Dove Cameron joins us
after the break.

00:08:09.834 --> 00:08:10.968
Stick around, everybody.

